@startuml layers-analytics
' Report §3.2 — analytics-service layers. On main this module is a skeleton: the four layer
' packages exist (each holds only a .gitkeep) and AnalyticsApplication is the only class.
' Second pass (M3): replace the notes with the topology beans, state-store query services and
' the analytics REST controller.
!pragma layout smetana
!include include/style.iuml
set separator ::
hide empty members

title analytics-service — layered architecture (au.edu.uow.csci318.conference.analytics)

class AnalyticsApplication <<@SpringBootApplication>>

package "api  (presentation layer)" as api <<api>> {
  class "(empty on main)" as api_empty
}
package "application  (service layer)" as application <<application>> {
  class "(empty on main)" as app_empty
}
package "domain  (domain layer)" as domain <<domain>> {
  class "(empty on main)" as dom_empty
}
package "infrastructure  (infrastructure layer)" as infrastructure <<infrastructure>> {
  class "(empty on main)" as inf_empty
}

AnalyticsApplication -[hidden]-> api
api -[hidden]-> application
application -[hidden]-> domain
domain -[hidden]-> infrastructure

note right of AnalyticsApplication
  Port 8085. application.yml sets only the port, the
  application name and logging: no datasource, no
  Kafka Streams binder configuration yet.
  This service will own <b>no database</b> — its state will
  live in Kafka Streams state stores (specs/5 §4).
end note

note right of infrastructure
  Planned for M3 (specs/5 §4), not on main:
  RT1 fill rate + 90% alert (FR-14, FR-15),
  RT2 gate throughput (FR-16),
  registration funnel — served by interactive queries.
end note
@enduml
